    STEP 4 — Permissions

		Ab AWS permissions ka page aayega.

		Tumhare Terraform ko initial infrastructure create karna hai:

        AdministratorAccess

        --OR--- 
		
		VPC
		EC2
		IAM
		EKS
		RDS
		ElastiCache
		S3
		ECR
		SSM
		Security Groups

		Agar tum specifically individual policies hi lagana chahte ho

		Tumhare listed services ke corresponding AWS managed policy names generally ye hain:

		Requirement	AWS Managed Policy
		EC2	- AmazonEC2FullAccess
		VPC	- AmazonVPCFullAccess
		IAM	- IAMFullAccess
		EKS	- AmazonEKSClusterPolicy / AmazonEKSServicePolicy (EKS permissions are more nuanced)
		RDS	- AmazonRDSFullAccess
		ElastiCache	- AmazonElastiCacheFullAccess
		S3	- AmazonS3FullAccess
		ECR	- AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryFullAccess
		SSM	- AmazonSSMFullAccess

		Tumhare current master.tf mein ye resources actually defined hain.

		Abhi lab/bootstrap ke liye simplest option:

		Permissions mein:

		  -- AdministratorAccess

		select kar sakte ho.

			Lekin sirf temporary bootstrap/lab purpose ke liye.

			Production mein hum isko replace karke least-privilege Terraform role banayenge.

